# L §2.2 rulebody: ["beats" LABEL {"," LABEL}] ["v" ID] ["governs" lspan] "=" …; L §5.11: a rule may state its own
# governs (`rule base governs 2028.. = …`), and applies at the law dates in it. The rule later governs from 2027 with no
# end: at law date 2026-06-30 base gives one = 1 (a), at 2027-06-30 later beats it, two = 2 (b). (A span with no end
# right before `=` was refused LOAD-PARSE before writer 8's second pass.)
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2027-12-31

source s "s"
input one: int
input two: int

def f: int at reader
  rule base = one
  rule later beats base governs 2027.. = two

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  one = 1
  two = 2

ask a: f law 2026-06-30
ask b: f law 2027-06-30
=== expect
a: 1
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-10-20
b: 2
  law date 2027-06-30, cut 2026-10-20
